Pearl

The interface follows MK Matrix (https://github.com/morrisonkuhlsen/mkmatrix): src/theme.rs,
src/icons.rs and src/widgets.rs, src/app/backstage.rs and the title bar in src/app.rs are adapted from it, Copyright (c) 2026
Morrison Kühlsen and the MK Matrix contributors, itself a fork of GridCraft, Copyright (c) 2026 ArtCraft
Team and the GridCraft contributors; all under MIT OR Apache-2.0. See LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE.
Real-time editing uses yrs (MIT) and snow (Apache-2.0 OR MIT).

Pearl carries none of ArtCraft's brand files and is not made or endorsed by the ArtCraft Team.

The Morrison Kühlsen name and wordmark in docs/brand/, shown on the splash screen, are Morrison Kühlsen
brand assets. They are not open source and are not covered by the licenses above; their terms are in
docs/brand/LICENSE.md.

The structure of src/splash.rs follows MK Perth's splash screen (MIT OR Apache-2.0). The picture in
assets/splash.png was supplied by the project's owner.

The message catalog code in src/i18n.rs is adapted from MK Perth (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

Typesetting is done by Typst (https://github.com/typst/typst), Apache-2.0. Pearl is not made or
endorsed by the Typst project.

Fonts in the interface (SIL Open Font License 1.1): Inter and JetBrains Mono; see assets/fonts/OFL-*.txt.

Fonts inside the program through Typst and the interface toolkit, unmodified: DejaVu Sans Mono, Foxit,
Libertinus Serif, New Computer Modern, Hack, Noto Emoji, Ubuntu and others, each under its own terms.
One of them, NewCM10-Regular, is under the GNU GPL version 3 or later with the Font Exception and the
Distribution Exception; its source is at https://ctan.org/pkg/newcomputermodern. That exception is what
keeps it from covering Pearl, as long as the font stays unmodified and Pearl stays under a licence
compatible with the GPL version 3.

Spell checking uses spellbook (MPL-2.0) and the VERO dictionary for Brazilian Portuguese, unmodified,
by Raimundo Santos Moura and his team, under the LGPLv3 and the Mozilla Public License; see assets/dict/pt_BR/
and https://pt-br.libreoffice.org/projetos/projeto-vero-verificador-ortografico/.

The full terms of everything above and of every package Pearl is built from are in
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, and in the program under Sobre o Pearl.
